## Install

**On this machine, from a local checkout:**

```bash
uv tool install .
```

**On any other machine (any OS), once this repo is pushed to GitHub — no
PyPI publish needed:**

```bash
{% if repository_url -%}
uv tool install "git+{{ repository_url }}.git"
{%- else -%}
uv tool install "git+https://github.com/<owner>/<repo>.git"
{%- endif %}
```

Pin a version/branch by appending `@<tag-or-branch>` to the URL. This is
also how an AI agent bootstraps this CLI on a fresh machine/sandbox where
it isn't installed yet — see `src/{{ package_name }}/data/SKILL.md`.

After install, the command `{{ package_name }}` is available globally, on
macOS, Linux and Windows alike (see `architecture.md` in the cli-generator
plugin for why: no shelling out, no hardcoded POSIX paths).

To pick up later architecture changes from the `cli-generator` template
itself, run `copier update` in this repo (requires this repo and the
template to both be git repos; see the `cli-generator` plugin's README).

## Architecture

This project follows a fixed CLI architecture:

- `src/{{ package_name }}/commands/` — argument parsing only, no business logic.
- `src/{{ package_name }}/core/` — services, models, errors: the real logic.
- `src/{{ package_name }}/providers/` — external APIs/integrations.
- `src/{{ package_name }}/credentials/` — secrets via the OS keychain (`keyring`)
  and environment variables. Secrets never live in `.{{ package_name }}/config.toml`.
- `src/{{ package_name }}/output/` — human (`rich`) and `--json` rendering.

Run `{{ package_name }} doctor` to check environment/config/auth readiness, and
`{{ package_name }} --help` for the full command surface. Every command supports
`--json` for machine/agent consumption.

See `src/{{ package_name }}/data/SKILL.md` for the agent-facing usage guide
bundled with this package — install it into an AI tool with
`{{ package_name }} skill install`, or get it as plain text with
`{{ package_name }} --ai` (works even without file access).
